= Mussolini Arrested!

Following the end of the latest elections, we have been informed that Benito Mussolini, head of the relatively unknown <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_full_italian +]</span> and former member of our own <span style="color:#ED2855">socialist</span> party, has been arrested in his hometown of Predappio, under allegation of harbouring illegal weapons as well as operating a violent organisation.

What should we do?

- @mussolini_justice: Keep him locked up and begin preparing for his trial.
- @root: Release him; don't let him become a martyr.

@mussolini_justice
subtitle: We can only hold him for so long. 
on-arrival: mussolini_jailed = 1; fdc_militancy += 0.08; fdc_strength += 7; mussolini_trial_timer = 12; veterans_pnf -= 3; middle_class_pnf -= 7; rural_pnf -= 4;

We keep Mussolini in prison, awaiting trial. His trial is to be in [+ mussolini_trial_timer +] months, and we should gather enough evidence to convict him by then.

In his absence however, the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci</span> grow more and more rowdy, terrorising the local populace and gaining a notorious reputation for themselves.

- @interior_investigations: Let's get to work then, shall we?

@interior_investigations
go-to: judiciary_reform